# Android Gray Flow — Native Kotlin Integration Guide

This is the canonical guide for building a **native Kotlin** gray-part app
(no Flutter). It mirrors the Flutter gray template but uses Activities, OkHttp,
the AppsFlyer Android SDK and Firebase Messaging directly.

---

## What is the gray flow

A dual-mode app:

- **Stream mode (online / "gray"):** a full-screen `WebView` shows a URL returned
  by a remote backend. The app is a thin shell.
- **Native mode (offline / "фантик" / white):** a real native game/content shown
  to organic / unattributed users.

The backend decides per user based on **AppsFlyer attribution**. Paid
(non-organic) users get the WebView; organic users get the native content.

**Why:** one binary, two experiences chosen at runtime. The native game is the
legitimate store-review content; the WebView delivers partner content to
targeted users only.

---

## Stealth principles (don't break these)

1. Real native game = real review content (reviewer/scanner sees the game).
2. XOR-encode all sensitive strings (config URL, AppsFlyer key, Firebase #,
   GCD URL). Never hardcode them at the call site.
3. Attribution gate: only paid installs see the WebView. A reviewer doing an
   organic install gets the game.
4. **Unique binary fingerprint per project** — different codec seed, class
   names, package layout, library versions. See `kotlin_fingerprint.mdc`.
5. Real device User-Agent on every request (no `; wv` / Flutter fingerprint).
   See `kotlin_webview.mdc`.

