## AppsFlyer attribution (the part most likely to be wrong)

**`kotlin_launch_flow.mdc` is the authority here.** The short version:

- `subscribeForDeepLink` + `init(key, listener, appContext)` in
  `Application.onCreate`; the listener goes INTO `init`, never registered after
  `start`. Bridge the callback to a coroutine with `CompletableDeferred`.
- `start(activity)` from the router, **after** connectivity is confirmed, and
  **with the Activity** — an application context passed from inside an activity
  does not trigger the SDK at all.
- Never let the SDK start offline: the failed conversion it caches is final for
  the session and turns a paid install into an organic one.
- Await the conversion and the deferred deep link in parallel.
- `af_status == "Organic"` may be a false positive on first run. Wait
  `~5s`, then call the **GCD API** and prefer its result:
  `GET <gcdBase><bundleId>?devkey=<devKey>&device_id=<appsFlyerUID>`. The
  dev key is a query parameter — in a header it is ignored and every call
  returns 400 (pitfalls #37). The same call is the fallback when the SDK
  reports nothing at all, so log its response **body**, or a broken request
  looks identical to an install AppsFlyer has not filed yet.
- Timeouts: first launch 30s, returning online 10s, deep-link 5s, re-ask 8s.
- NEVER modify the conversion field set.

